  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={x\\in Z\u2223x\\le 5}$ and $B={x\\in Z\u2223-7\\le x<3}?$\n\n- $A\u2286B$\n- $B\u2286A$\n- $B\u2288A$\n- $A\u2287B$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all the integer numbers that satisfy the inequality $x\\le 5.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nA={\u2026,-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are all integers that satisfy the inequality $-7\\le x<3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nB={-7,-6,-5,-4,-3,-2,-1,0,1,2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A\u2286B$ is false.  For example, $5\\in A$ but $5\\notin B.$\n\n- $B\u2286A$ is true, while $B\u2288A$ is false. Every element in the set $B$ is an element of the set $A.$\n\n- $A\u2287B$ is equivalent to $B\u2286A,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only\".",
